      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "The application of Jenkins activity survey allowed to assess the behavior pattern of 76 managers (white collar workers) exposed to professional stress. In 54-82% of the subjects the type A behavioral pattern was found; conventional risk factors for coronary heart disease existed in more than 50% of the cases. Individual advices to prevent or restrain the coronary risk were given."},
